# 2. FINAL FEATURE SCOPE

## MANDATORY CORE

### 1. Crop Disease Detection

The user uploads a crop/leaf image.

The system must:

* Accept an image
* Preprocess the image
* Run the trained computer-vision model
* Predict the disease class or healthy class
* Return confidence
* Display the result clearly
* Provide basic precautionary guidance
* Provide appropriate uncertainty handling

The disease model must be independent from Gemini.

Gemini must NOT replace the disease-classification model.

Architecture:

Image
→ preprocessing
→ trained CV model
→ disease prediction
→ confidence
→ precaution/recommendation layer
→ frontend

The core must support a required prediction interface such as:

predict(image_path) → class_label

or an equivalent documented CLI/API.

The model must be evaluated honestly.

Do not train on the organizers' held-out judging test set.

The primary metric is macro-F1 on the held-out field-condition test set.

Also report:

* Confusion matrix
* Per-class precision
* Per-class recall
* Accuracy where appropriate
* Baseline comparison
* Limitations/failure cases

The challenge intentionally tests generalization from laboratory-style training images to field-condition images. Therefore, focus on generalization rather than artificially maximizing training accuracy.

